## Stack
Next.js 16 App Router · React 19 · TypeScript · Tailwind v4 (`@theme` in `globals.css`) · Firebase Admin (Firestore, keyless ADC) · nodemailer → Gmail SMTP · App Hosting auto-deploy on `main`.

## How access works TODAY
1. **Gate ON in prod** (`ACCESS_GATE_ENABLED=true` in `apphosting.yaml`). Unauthenticated visitors are **rewritten to `/apply`**.
2. **`/apply`** = sole info-form gateway (Instant mode: submit → session cookie → site). TCPA consent required. Persists `doctor-applications` + mints invite + emails admin (full detail).
3. **Password `/locked` flow PAUSED** (2026-07-07) but code kept. Restore via commented block in `src/proxy.ts`.
4. **Team one-click `?c=CODE` ENABLED** (2026-07-09): shared "Team" invite link skips the form. Trade-off: no per-person attribution; rotate whole code if leaked.
5. **Landing CTA** = **"Be Considered" button** → `POST /api/consider` (not the old multi-field form). Looks up doctor from session → emails Mel. Legacy form copy kept in `content.ts`.
6. **`/admin`** = Mel invite mint/list/revoke (`ADMIN_SECRET`). CLI: `node scripts/invite.mjs`.

